# Deezer API — Quick Reference

Deezer exposes a public REST API with no authentication required for catalog
search and metadata. All endpoints return JSON by default.

Base URL: `https://api.deezer.com`

---

## Search by artist name

Returns a ranked list of artist matches. Use this to resolve an artist to its
numeric `id`.

```
GET https://api.deezer.com/search/artist?q=<query>
```

Top result example:

```json
{
  "id": 1590752,
  "name": "Young Thug",
  "nb_fan": 1552508,
  "nb_album": 141
}
```

Fields returned:
- `id` — Deezer artist ID
- `name` — Artist name
- `nb_fan` — Number of listeners / followers
- `nb_album` — Number of albums / releases

---

## Search tracks by artist + title

General track search. Combine artist and title in the query string.
Results include nested `album` and `artist` objects with their own `id` and
`title`.

```
GET https://api.deezer.com/search?q=<query>
```

Example query:

```
https://api.deezer.com/search?q=wyclef%20jean%20young%20thug
```

Top result:

```json
{
  "id": 130914062,
  "title": "Wyclef Jean",
  "artist": { "id": 1590752, "name": "Young Thug" },
  "album":  { "id": 13899072, "title": "JEFFERY" }
}
```

### Advanced query syntax

You can scope terms to specific fields with `field:value` (quotes around
space-containing values):

```
GET https://api.deezer.com/search?q=track:"wyclef jean" artist:"young thug"
```

Note: Deezer's advanced field filtering can be unreliable for exact matches
(the above may return zero results). The general `q=` free-text approach
is more reliable.

---

## Get full track metadata

The search response omits `release_date`, `duration`, and `genre_id` for
individual tracks. Fetch the full track object to get these:

```
GET https://api.deezer.com/track/<track_id>
```

Fields:

```json
{
  "id": 130914062,
  "title": "Wyclef Jean",
  "duration": 236,
  "track_position": 1,
  "release_date": "2016-08-26",
  "artist": { "id": 1590752, "name": "Young Thug" },
  "album": {
    "id": 13899072,
    "title": "JEFFERY",
    "release_date": "2016-08-26"
  }
}
```

Key fields:
- `duration` — Track length in seconds
- `track_position` — Track number on the album
- `release_date` — Inherited from album

---

## Get full album metadata (incl. genre)

Genre info lives on the album object, not the track. Fetch it separately:

```
GET https://api.deezer.com/album/<album_id>
```

```json
{
  "id": 13899072,
  "title": "JEFFERY",
  "release_date": "2016-08-26",
  "label": "300 Entertainment/Atl",
  "record_type": "album",
  "explicit_lyrics": true,
  "genres": {
    "data": [
      { "id": 116, "name": "Rap/Hip Hop" }
    ]
  }
}
```

Key fields:
- `genres.data[].name` — List of genre names (array of objects with `id` and `name`)
- `label` — Record label
- `record_type` — e.g. `album`, `single`, `ep`
- `explicit_lyrics` — `true` / `false`

---

## Summary of endpoints used

| Step                       | Endpoint                                           |
|----------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| Resolve artist by name     | `GET /search/artist?q=<name>`                      |
| Search tracks by title     | `GET /search?q=<artist+title>`                     |
| Full track metadata        | `GET /track/<track_id>`                            |
| Full album + genre metadata| `GET /album/<album_id>`                            |

## Worked example

Target: find album name, genre, and release date for the song
"Wyclef Jean" by Young Thug.

1. Search tracks:

```bash
curl -s "https://api.deezer.com/search?q=wyclef%20jean%20young%20thug"
```

   → First result has `id: 130914062`, `album.id: 13899072`.

2. Fetch album:

```bash
curl -s "https://api.deezer.com/album/13899072"
```

   Result:

   - Album: JEFFERY
   - Release date: 2016-08-26
   - Genre: Rap/Hip Hop
